From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:01:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rga: Register the video device after binding
 the cores

rga_bind() registers the video device before it binds the cores. When
component_bind_all() fails, the error path frees the registered video
device with video_device_release(). The freed video device is still on
the devices_kset list and on dpm_list, and still in sysfs, in the cdev
table and in video_devices[], so every later walk of those lists or
lookup of the node uses freed memory.

On an RK3588 boot where the IOMMUs probe late, binding the second RGA3
core failed with -ENODEV ("Couldn't get domain of the first core") and
took this path. A video device registered after that got the same
2 KiB slab object back, so the object went into both lists a second
time while the lists were still linked through the stale entry. When
the IOMMU of the second core probed, device_link_add() moved that core,
the entry just before the stale one, to the tail of the lists, and
both list checks fired:

  list_del corruption. next->prev should be ffff00010144e818,
    but was ffff00010144a818. (next=ffff000107bc00c0)
  list_del corruption. next->prev should be ffff00010144e900,
    but was ffff00010144a900. (next=ffff000107bc01a8)
   devices_kset_move_last / device_pm_move_last
   device_reorder_to_tail
   device_link_add
   rk_iommu_probe_device

The "next" entries are kobj.entry and power.entry of a struct
video_device, which keeps its struct device at offset 0xb8.

Register the video device last, after all cores are bound, the way the
driver did before it was split into a master and cores. Userspace also
cannot open the node before the cores are bound and the parallel job
limit is set. If the registration fails, unbind the cores again.

Fixes: 947bd9f26316 ("media: rockchip: rga: move video device to the master")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c
index bfda077a0f44..91642fd7d79d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c
@@ -1132,12 +1132,6 @@ static int rga_bind(struct device *dev)
 		goto rel_vdev;
 	}
 
-	ret = video_register_device(vfd, VFL_TYPE_VIDEO, -1);
-	if (ret) {
-		v4l2_err(&rga->v4l2_dev, "Failed to register video device\n");
-		goto rel_m2m;
-	}
-
 	ret = component_bind_all(dev, rga);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "component bind failed\n");
@@ -1147,11 +1141,24 @@ static int rga_bind(struct device *dev)
 	/* after binding all cores num_cores has the proper number of cores */
 	v4l2_m2m_set_max_parallel_jobs(rga->m2m_dev, rga->num_cores);
 
+	/*
+	 * Register the video device last, once all cores are bound: a
+	 * registered video device must not be freed with
+	 * video_device_release().
+	 */
+	ret = video_register_device(vfd, VFL_TYPE_VIDEO, -1);
+	if (ret) {
+		v4l2_err(&rga->v4l2_dev, "Failed to register video device\n");
+		goto unbind_cores;
+	}
+
 	v4l2_info(&rga->v4l2_dev, "Registered %s as /dev/%s\n",
 		  vfd->name, video_device_node_name(vfd));
 
 	return 0;
 
+unbind_cores:
+	component_unbind_all(dev, NULL);
 rel_m2m:
 	v4l2_m2m_release(rga->m2m_dev);
 rel_vdev:
